-- title:
--   Tᵣ is congruent mod p to Hecke operators away from r
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and suppose that the weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ have an integral structure in the sense of [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6), i.e. the complex span of the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule generated by those cusp forms all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are rational integers is the whole space. Let $p$ and $r$ be primes with $r \neq p$ and $r \nmid N$, and let $S$ be a finite set of natural numbers with $r \notin S$. For a set $S$ of natural numbers, [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) denotes the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` attached to the primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators `heckeULin` attached to the primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$. The assertion is that there exist an element $t'$ of [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 (insert r S)`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) and an element $t''$ of [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) such that the Hecke operator $T_r$ on $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$, namely [`CuspForm.heckeTLin 2 hr hrN`](def/ModularForm_HeckeOperatorForms.html#L69) viewed as a $\mathbb{C}$-linear endomorphism, satisfies $T_r = t' + p \cdot t''$.
--
--   This is the first of the two claims in Wiles's proof of Ribet's lemma on generation of the Hecke ring: modulo $p$, the operator $T_r$ at a prime $r \neq p$ with $r \nmid N$ already lies in the subring generated by the remaining Hecke operators, so that the inclusion $\mathbb{T}^{S \cup \{r\}}(N) \subseteq \mathbb{T}^{S}(N)$ is surjective after reduction modulo $p$. It is used in [`CuspForm.exists_not_dvd_and_smul_mem_heckeAlgebra_of_finite`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_not_dvd_and_smul_mem_heckeAlgebra_of_finite) and in [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.exists_ringHom_apply_T_eq_of_insert_of_residue_eq`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.exists_ringHom_apply_T_eq_of_insert_of_residue_eq), which remove a finite set of primes from the list of generators of the Hecke algebra.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_exists_mem_heckeAlgebra_insert_heckeTLin_eq_add_smul_of_ne.lean

import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_IntegralStructure

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

theorem CuspForm.exists_mem_heckeAlgebra_insert_heckeTLin_eq_add_smul_of_ne
    (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (hint : CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2)
    (p r : ℕ) (hp : p.Prime) (hr : r.Prime) (hrp : r ≠ p) (hrN : ¬ r ∣ N)
    (S : Set ℕ) (hS : S.Finite) (hrS : r ∉ S) :
    ∃ t' ∈ CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 (insert r S),
      ∃ t'' ∈ CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S,
        (CuspForm.heckeTLin 2 hr hrN :
            Module.End ℂ (CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) 2)) = t' + (p : ℤ) • t'' := by sorry
